@page "/vek/community/reporting-bugs"

<DocsPage DisplayFooter="true">
    <DocsPageHeader Title="Reporting Bugs" SubTitle="" />
    <DocsPageContent>
        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Make sure an issue is the right place">
                <Description>
                    Use a bug report when Vek behaves differently from its documented or expected behavior. If you are unsure how to use a feature, need help with setup, or want advice about an approach, visit our <VekLink Href="/vek/community/getting-help">Getting Help</VekLink> page instead. The community can help you work out whether you have found a defect.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Look for an existing report">
                <Description>
                    Search the <VekLink Href="https://github.com/madiseh/vek/issues" Target="_blank">Vek issues</VekLink> before opening a new report. If someone has already reported the same behavior, add a comment with any details that can help investigate it, such as another reproduction or environment. This keeps related information together and avoids duplicate reports.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Show how to reproduce it">
                <Description>
                    A small, self-contained example helps the team reproduce the behavior and identify its cause. Try it in <VekLink Href="https://try.vek.com" Target="_blank">TryVek</VekLink> first and include the snippet link in your report. If the issue depends on your host or project setup, share a minimal public repository that demonstrates it rather than a complete application.
                    <br/><br/>
                    In your report, describe what you expected and what happened, list the steps that trigger the problem, and include the Vek version and relevant environment details. Add any error messages that clarify the failure, and remove secrets or private data from examples.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <VekButton DropShadow="false" EndIcon="@Icons.Material.Rounded.OpenInNew" Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Class="docs-no-text-transform" Href="https://github.com/madiseh/vek/issues/new/choose" Target="_blank">Report a bug on GitHub</VekButton>
        </DocsPageSection>

    </DocsPageContent>
</DocsPage>
